---
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/contracts-ports-dark.svg?raw';
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/contracts-ports-light.svg?raw';
import Diagram from './Diagram.astro';
---

<Diagram
  lightSvg={lightSvg}
  darkSvg={darkSvg}
  maxWidth={680}
  caption="The station's five ports. One setting picks the whole column: every port is a mock, or every port is real, never a mix."
>
  A three-column table of the inspection station's five ports, each with its
  mock and its real adapter. Order lookup asks which tapes are in a box: the
  mock answers from three sample orders plus orders generated per test, the
  real adapter makes one GET to the order service per scan. Media locator asks
  where each file is: the mock serves bundled test clips and keeps capture
  versions in a JSON file, the real adapter calls the media service to locate
  once per order and refresh per file. Inspection sink saves a result: the mock
  appends to a file and refuses what production refuses, the real adapter
  posts to the inspection API, which deduplicates by event ID. Inspection
  reader asks what any station has saved: the mock reads the same file back,
  the real adapter reads the inspection API back by order. Notify
  sink posts the order summary: the mock appends to a log file, the real
  adapter posts one Slack message per finished round.
</Diagram>
